      "writtenOn": "2025-06-27T01:58:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In my opinion, it would be easy for users to configure the dl_server flag to determine whether to use the scaled (dl_server \u003d 0) or non-scaled (dl_server \u003d 1) mode. \n\nNow since the rq-\u003efair_server.dl_server is 1 at dl_server_start, now it\u0027s always use non-sclaed.\n\nMoreover,You can refer this discuss, (Add a deadline server for sched_ext tasks )\nI think maintainer want to use server argument than a specific server. It still under discuss.\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/all/20250620203234.3349930-8-joelagnelf@nvidia.com/\n\nSo I think we should use the server argument rather than the dl_server flag to align with their future changes.",
      "parentUuid": "c38e708e_54a5dc08",
      "revId": "6bdcf1b3d203a740d85948bbf1d160fa357fc5f2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
